= Women's Rights

According to the Constitution, women are equal to men, but this is not followed in practice. Women in the workforce are not paid equally for the same work, in addition to often being pushed out of employment after marriage. Men are still favored in marriage and family policy, and there are restrictions on women's rights in many other domains. And that is not to mention the overwhelming patriarchal culture present in Germany.

Few parties take this as seriously as our own. Bäumer and Lüders have made women's civic and economic equality a central part of our platform since the party's founding. However, The question has never been whether we care about this. It is how far we are willing to spend our limited political capital pushing it. 

- @labor: Institute policies that help women in the workforce.
- @family: Reform marriage, divorce, and property law.
- @welfare: Improve welfare for single mothers and children.
- @liberalize: Attempt to liberalize abortion laws.
- @return: Do not enact any policies for now.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@labor
subtitle: Paid maternal leave policies, equal pay policies, and so on.
on-arrival: womens_work += 1; womens_rights += 1; linksliberale_strength += 3; linksliberale_dissent -= 3 if linksliberale_dissent > 0; new_middle_ddp += 5*(1-dissent); workers_ddp += 2*(1-dissent); economic_growth += 0.1
max-visits: 3

These policies mean our party's standing continues to grow among the "new women" entering white-collar and professional work. [? if unemployed > 15 : However, many male workers develop a backlash towards women in the workplace, especially given the rising unemployment. ?]

@family
subtitle: Change family and inheritance law to treat women more equally.
on-arrival: family_law += 1; womens_rights += 1; linksliberale_strength += 2; new_middle_ddp += 4*(1-dissent); old_middle_ddp -= 2*(1-dissent); rural_ddp -= 2*(1-dissent); catholics_ddp -= 3*(1-dissent); coalition_dissent += 1; z_relation -= 5
max-visits: 2

These policies aim to ensure that women have equal rights within a marriage, including the right to divorce. The more conservative segments of society treat our reforms as deleterious to the social fabric.


@welfare
subtitle: -1 budget
choose-if: budget > 0
on-arrival: welfare += 1; new_middle_ddp += 4*(1-dissent); linksliberale_strength += 2; budget -= 1; womens_rights += 1; coalition_dissent += 1 if welfare >= 1 and unemployed >= 15; unemployed -= 0.4; inflation += 0.2; economic_growth += 0.3

We have increased welfare spending on women and children. [? if welfare >= 1 and unemployed >= 15 : Some of our coalition partners consider increased welfare spending profligate at this time. ?]


@liberalize
max-visits: 1
subtitle: [? if progressive_coalition < 50 : This is unlikely to succeed; we do not have majority support. ?]
go-to: liberalize_fail if progressive_coalition < 50; liberalize_success if progressive_coalition >= 50

@liberalize_fail
on-arrival: z_relation -= 5; coalition_dissent += 1; linksliberale_dissent += 4; new_middle_ddp += 2*(1-dissent); catholics_ddp -= 4*(1-dissent)

Unfortunately, our proposal is voted down in the Reichstag, with the Catholic Center party (our long-time partners) speaking in particularly vehement opposition, and some of our own members breaking party discipline. Bäumer's activists, demoralized, decide to bide their time for a more favorable moment.

@liberalize_success
on-arrival: abortion_rights += 1; womens_rights += 1; linksliberale_strength += 3; coalition_dissent += 1; z_relation -= 8; catholics_ddp -= 8*(1-dissent); dvp_relation -= 5; new_middle_ddp += 8*(1-dissent); workers_ddp += 4*(1-dissent); workers_z += 3; new_middle_z += 3; old_middle_z += 3; old_middle_dnvp += 3; rural_dnvp += 3; workers_nsdap -= 5; new_middle_nsdap -= 7; old_middle_nsdap -= 2; rural_nsdap -= 2; unemployed_nsdap -= 2

With the support of a "progressive coalition" including the SPD and, unlikely, the KPD, we have successfully passed a bill to legalize abortion in Germany! It heartens our most progressive supporters and fulfills everything Bäumer and Lüders have argued for years, while hurting our relations with the Center Party. With the increasing political discourse around abortion, the religiously-oriented Center Party and DNVP have gained conservative votes at the expense of the NSDAP.
